<title>UK: Royal Bank close to Midshires deal -paper.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank close to Midshires deal -paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Royal Bank of Scotland will announce a 650 million stg takeover of Birmingham Midshires building society &quot;within the next few weeks&quot;, The Daily Telegraph reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The report said the one million members of Birmingham Midshires, Britain's fifth largest building society, could expect 'windfall' bonuses averaging around 800 stg each from the deal.</p>
<p>The society suspended new account openings last week, saying it had been swamped by speculators opening accounts in order to receive windfalls. More than 300,000 new investors have opened accounts over the past year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
